Adapted from xerj-org/xerj (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj)

The `_bulk` push semantics — `index` action with `version_type: external` and
`version` set to the source document's `_seq_no`, so that a full rerun after
an interruption always converges instead of duplicating writes — and the
retry/fail-fast classification of target responses (transient: transport
error, 5xx, 429, 408 — retried with capped exponential backoff and jitter;
permanent: any other 4xx — reported immediately, not retried) are adapted
from xerj's single-node WAL tap:

  https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/blob/main/engine/crates/xerj-engine/src/wal_tap.rs

The `target_url` validation (rejecting embedded userinfo, e.g.
`user:pass@host`, because an HTTP client turns it into an `Authorization`
header behind the caller's back) and the redaction of credentials from any
echoed/logged output are adapted from:

  https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/blob/main/engine/crates/xerj-api/src/wal_tap_api.rs

No code from xerj was copied verbatim; the patterns above were reimplemented
in this project's own Rust source. See README.md's Attribution section for
more detail.
